@preamble let cases = import("string/case_table")
upper_rune
Returns the Unicode simple upper-case mapping for rune r. This internal module
backs string/native; ordinary programs should use string.upper_rune.

upper_rune(r)

cases.upper_rune('a')    # 'A'
===
lower_rune
Returns the Unicode simple lower-case mapping for rune r. This internal module
backs string/native; ordinary programs should use string.lower_rune.

lower_rune(r)

cases.lower_rune('A')    # 'a'
